WEBVTT

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.980
We're still not there?

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.690
Just a little more!

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:36.910
Stop!

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.510
I'm sorry.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.560
Don't worry about it.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.600
Come on. Say sorry.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.100
Sorry.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.110
It's okay.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.610
Bound for Tokyo and Shinagawa

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:53.610
The next station is Ebisu

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.600
Bye-bye!

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.440
It's okay...

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:08.520
It's okay...

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:17.760
Crossing at Twilight 2

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.830
It was really amazing!

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.770
Like a festival!

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.070
Did you go to Odaiba with your boyfriend?

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:35.530
Yeah, but Himura was nagging me to go book a hotel room the whole time.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.520
That's so gross!

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.910
And did you go?

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.070
Of course not!

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.040
It's not my fault...

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.690
What should I do?

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:51.910
Nothing. They've always been like that.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.070
But...

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.430
Ugh, that sounds bad.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:09.190
Her boyfriend holding hands with his old crush of all people...

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:12.090
She didn't come to the meeting place,

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.410
she's not picking up her phone, and she's not replying to my texts either.

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.380
What the hell's going on?!

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.950
Is this hotel really in reception range?!

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.410
I bet I've already missed a dozen calls!

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.190
That hurt...

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.600
The hell are you doing?

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.670
That's my line!

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.850
What do you think you're doing?!

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:43.500
A man whining over his bloody phone?!

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:57.440
I'll... try going to her place.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:02.930
You can't get out through the front. The teacher's watching too.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:07.000
Then how about the emergency stairs?

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.420
You should get out through the parking lot from there.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.880
Okay, then just in case, I'll distract the teacher!

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.200
Sounds like a perfect plan to me!

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.720
You're gonna help me?

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.750
Well, if there's something in it for me, maybe I'll help.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.040
I want something to drink!

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.450
I want ice cream!

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.110
The Häagen-Dazs green tea flavor special!

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.510
You have until 10 PM, which is when the teacher will come to check if we're sleeping.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:42.200
Go and make up with her!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.720
I sure as hell don't want to leave like this!

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:57.210
I don't care how mad she is,

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.540
I don't care how much she'll hate me,

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.800
I want to see her.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.890
I want to see her...

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.060
I want to see her!

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:17.270
I guess they've met by now. Haruto and Yuzuki, I mean.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.310
Yeah, I guess.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:24.030
Those two are kinda bound by the red string of fate.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:28.280
Gee, that's so out of character coming from you. Creepy!

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.750
Shut up!

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:32.040
You? Talking about the red string of fate?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.290
Oh Takashi! Whatever, just get me that for a moment.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:38.920
Eba

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.010
I'm out of my mind. What am I doing?

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.900
Haruto?!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.900
I'm so surprised!

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:06.120
I almost called the police on this creepy guy hanging around my house!

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:09.910
We're here on a school trip now. Would you call her for me?

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.100
I forgot my phone.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:18.670
I met my sister earlier on my way home.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.480
Where did she go?

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.470
How should I know?

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:27.680
I have no idea what goes on in her mind.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:33.560
What if she has a boyfriend and she's going on a date?

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.560
Long-distance relationships don't last long.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.990
I believe in her!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:44.430
Sure, feel free to...

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:47.950
But please call her!

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.420
You're worrying too much.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.950
Don't worry. She'll come back eventually.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.710
I wouldn't mind if she didn't, though.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:01.760
Isn't she always like this?

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:06.000
She charms the pants off you by acting like a klutz.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.660
She's just trying to catch your fancy.

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.470
Just watching that pisses me off.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:16.180
What are you talking about? She's—

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:29.240
Just watching you pisses me off too.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:37.030
How long are you going to stand there?

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:42.750
I'll call the police about our stalker problem.

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:23.250
The Tokyo night...

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:33.490
It's so bright, but I can't find her.

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.800
Just give up.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.460
We don't have time either, so let's hurry back.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.520
Yeah...

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:46.270
Have you heard the meeting place changed?

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:50.000
You're worrying too much.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:54.030
Don't worry. She'll come back eventually.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.270
No chance!

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:57.410
Yeah right!

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.920
I wouldn't mind if she didn't, though.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.590
I'm from Tokyo. My name is Eba Yuzuki.

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:10.880
Nice to meet you!

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:15.610
Why would you come to some high school at the ends of the Earth?

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:18.190
Your parents must've been worried too.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:24.390
Yes, but it's my father's homeland, and it's okay if I stay at a friend's place.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:29.280
And you're really beautiful too!

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:30.480
<i>After she came to Hiroshima, Eba was trying to find her place.</i>

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:30.480
Thank you!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.400
I can't!

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:41.910
I can't do anything if you're not around!

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:45.880
But I didn't realize at all.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.500
I'm not getting on.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:49.890
What?!

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:52.510
I'm going back with you.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.510
I don't want to go to Tokyo.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.650
She was just being stubborn...

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.970
I chased my sister off.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:05.370
I don't consider her my sister, though.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.490
She just endured...

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:16.490
Hello?

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.450
Where are you, Eba?

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.910
Right...

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.230
behind you...

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:27.790
She just forced herself to smile.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:43.400
My father remarried.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:48.330
Rin and my brother are Mother's children.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:54.440
That's why our relationship is kinda... strained.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:58.160
But we're family...

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.780
I'm telling you I'm your family too.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.370
But if it's hard on you, let it show on your face.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:10.380
Then I'll help you if I can.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:21.260
But I must be there for her...

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:30.440
At the very least, I must be a steady, safe point in her life.

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:36.020
Yet...

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.230
You're late!

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:18.990
You're late!

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.980
I texted you to say I was going to meet you,

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:30.580
but you forgot your phone...

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:35.460
I even went to your hotel! I spent so much time looking for you!

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:40.530
I kinda know what happened with Nanami.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:44.640
But seeing that anyone would think—

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:53.030
I wanted to see you.

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:56.560
I wanted to see you so badly.

00:11:59.170 --> 00:12:02.430
I wanted to see you all this time.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:09.920
This isn't fair.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.370
I'm glad we could meet in the end.

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:20.200
I was going to go home if you didn't come in five minutes.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:21.760
I see...

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:24.270
What's wrong?

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.350
It's just...

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.740
Haruto?

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:35.770
I'm sorry.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:40.970
I promised I'd never make you sad...

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:45.220
But then I let you see that...

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:48.020
I'm really...

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:51.540
...really sorry.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.590
It's okay.

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:55.690
But...

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:57.390
Don't waste time on that.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.300
I want to talk to you about other stuff too.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.070
I'm sorry, Eba.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:27.820
I'm stupid, insensitive, and I fail at being straightforward.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.120
So beautiful!

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:42.840
By the way...

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:43.840
Hm?

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:46.330
Why would you come to this city?

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.270
It ain't something you just decide on a whim.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:53.080
Usually people don't <i>want</i> to leave Tokyo for a countryside school.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:03.190
I've been to this town just once, a long time ago.

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.270
I really liked it back then.

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:07.820
That's all?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.050
Yeah.

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:10.980
That's weird!

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:12.300
Not at all!

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.790
No, it really—

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:14.960
Does it matter?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:25.910
Just leave it at that.

00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:36.550
I'm stupid, insensitive, and I fail at being straightforward.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:44.910
I think from the moment we met...

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.000
I've loved you.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:54.740
I think from the moment we met...

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.250
All this time.

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:10.270
I've loved you for such a long time.

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:20.770
Mom, buy that!

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:21.770
Thanks, Akari!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:23.550
Hey, Satoshi, wait!

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:32.860
Hey!

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.310
Are you lost?

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:42.980
What's your name?

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:44.980
I can't tell you.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.300
Why?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:50.800
I don't want to go home.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.360
What? Why?

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:57.570
I didn't want to come here at all!

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:03.620
Hey, don't cry!

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:09.160
I've no choice, huh?

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:13.210
I'll show you a nice place.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.860
A nice place?

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.180
Is this the nice place?

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:27.040
Yeah.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:32.170
You know, flowers bloom on the lake once a year.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.450
But there are no flowers...

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:44.690
There it is!

00:16:57.890 --> 00:16:58.960
How is it?

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.080
They're on the lake too, aren't they?

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:03.390
They're huge!

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:09.840
So beautiful!

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.340
Thank you!

00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.590
You finally smiled.

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.290
Do you like the town now?

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.530
Yeah!

00:17:25.530 --> 00:17:27.140
Then don't cry.

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:31.570
But something bad happened to me.

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:35.240
But now I feel like it'll be okay!

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:36.740
I see.

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:47.050
Then if something happens, just come again!

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:48.560
Can I?

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:49.330
Sure.

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:55.340
Promise.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:17:59.880
Sure.

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.120
It's a promise.

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:11.870
Here, it's yours.

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.530
I couldn't get you anything for your birthday.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.370
Darn, I got you something too!

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.060
I left it at the hotel.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.480
Don't worry about it.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:29.870
But it's not right for a boyfriend to just take...

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:40.860
It's about time.

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.390
Don't go back to Tokyo.

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:52.550
Don't go back, and just stay here with me.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.400
I can't.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:58.110
Feelings change.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:18:59.770
But...

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:02.000
They really do.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:06.900
You loved Nanami so much until just recently.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.700
Feelings change.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.040
I can't handle a long-distance relationship.

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:21.130
Then it doesn't have to be long-distance!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.890
If you're so worried...

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:28.990
I'll go to Tokyo too!

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:46.660
Don't be stupid.

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:51.360
Even if you did, it wouldn't be easier.

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.360
Actually, I was really happy

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.000
that you said you want to go out with me,

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:34.370
that you said you'd come to Tokyo...

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:37.890
I...

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.660
I want to stay with you.

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:57.860
This isn't enough.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:01.720
You...

00:21:03.070 --> 00:21:04.430
You must go.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.060
This is goodbye, then. Say hi to the others for me.

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:13.370
Yeah.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.870
The more you look forward to meeting someone,

00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:21.270
the tougher it will be to say goodbye.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:25.060
Something wrong?

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:26.760
No...

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:31.220
It's just really tough...

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:33.830
Over the distance...

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.180
Then should we break up?

00:21:39.010 --> 00:21:41.100
Don't even joke about that!

00:21:46.790 --> 00:21:49.280
Take care, Haruto.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:52.540
See you later.

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:04.310
I'll...

00:22:09.770 --> 00:22:11.300
I'll come to meet you again.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:12.780
It's a promise.

00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:24.760
Yeah. It's a promise.

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:36.800
This!

00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:40.580
This Amami restaurant's rice omelet was super great!

00:22:41.810 --> 00:22:43.430
It looks delicious!

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:47.040
And the waitress was friggin' <i>hot</i> too!

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:49.010
I want to see her again!

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:52.850
Then go to Tokyo alone!

00:22:52.850 --> 00:22:55.410
I will! Haruto, you will too, right?

00:22:56.260 --> 00:22:57.850
Yeah, I will.

00:22:58.610 --> 00:23:00.830
You weren't listening, were you?

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:02.480
No, I was.

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:06.540
Nanami, you say something too!

00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:10.990
But that's... Um... You know...

00:23:07.710 --> 00:23:10.130
For a while we'll be far apart,

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:12.800
Haruto's going nuts.

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:14.740
but we'll be fine for sure.

00:23:12.800 --> 00:23:14.750
His head is just full of Yuzuki.

00:23:15.750 --> 00:23:20.250
Our hearts are connected, bridging time and space.

00:23:23.890 --> 00:23:26.000
Our long distance relationship

00:23:30.140 --> 00:23:32.890
just begun.

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:43.290
Rushing to me at the crossing at twilight

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:51.130
That feeling that I want to see you

00:23:51.840 --> 00:23:58.010
Like the clouds swimming in the sky

00:23:58.800 --> 00:24:05.310
Meeting, melting and disappearing

00:24:06.560 --> 00:24:13.320
For a while we've been ignoring each other

00:24:13.690 --> 00:24:16.950
But to be honest I'm still

00:24:17.490 --> 00:24:24.410
seeking only you

00:24:24.790 --> 00:24:28.000
My wish to see you

00:24:28.330 --> 00:24:32.130
is eternally painted in the sky

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:35.340
See, today again it's all so

00:24:35.630 --> 00:24:38.470
dazzling and lovely

00:24:38.470 --> 00:24:41.560
Standing in a sunny place,

00:24:41.930 --> 00:24:46.140
like a blooming sunflower,

00:24:46.140 --> 00:24:52.520
I keep looking at my shining love.
